# TEMPLATE for the PRIVATE overlay repository (fictional; docs/private-overlay.md "Branch
# protection").  Replace @lab-owner-fake with your GitHub user (or a team).  With "Require review
# from Code Owners" on main's branch protection, a pull request that changes how the lab is
# checked or deployed needs the owner's approval: the required `checks` job runs the workflow
# from the pull request itself, so without this a pull request could rewrite checks.yml to pass.
# While you are the only writer, GitHub cannot let you approve your own pull request: merge as
# admin (the rule binds everyone else) and turn the bypass off when a second writer joins.
#
# Deny by default: the first rule owns every path, so a path added later (or one the lines below
# leave out: the inventory and known_hosts that pick the deploy's targets, lab/customizations/
# whose hooks run tasks, the sealed files) needs the owner's review too.  GitHub applies the LAST
# matching rule, so a line below may name a narrower owner but must never name none.  The lines
# below say why each path matters; they are kept for that, not for coverage.
*                             @lab-owner-fake

# the workflows, and this file
/.github/                     @lab-owner-fake
# what the deploy runs, with what tools, and the runner's job-started hook
/bin/                         @lab-owner-fake
/runner/                      @lab-owner-fake
/ansible.cfg                  @lab-owner-fake
/ansible/playbooks/           @lab-owner-fake
# which hosts the deploy reaches, as whom and through what (ansible_host, ssh args, become), and
# the host keys it trusts
/ansible/inventory/           @lab-owner-fake
/ansible/known_hosts          @lab-owner-fake
/locks/                       @lab-owner-fake
# what the lab claims as its own: the site's delegated IPv6 prefixes (a model runtime's lab-only
# rule trusts them), its zones, egress, firewall allows and tailnet, and the selection's scope and
# grants (hnx site review-tier, in checks.yml, rates each widening human-approve)
/lab/site.yml                 @lab-owner-fake
/lab/modules.yml              @lab-owner-fake
# what the rest of the lab trusts (hnx site review-tier rates every change to these human-approve):
# the registry every svc: allow renders to, the guests' zones, addresses and outbound allows, and
# the overlay's own modules and the lock that pins the fetched ones, and the model role table
# (a binding's leaves_lab and a role's fallback decide who needs grants.cloud_models) with the
# swap records that cover a change to it
/lab/services.yml             @lab-owner-fake
/lab/guests/                  @lab-owner-fake
/lab/modules/                 @lab-owner-fake
/lab/modules.lock             @lab-owner-fake
/lab/model_roles.json         @lab-owner-fake
/lab/swaps/                   @lab-owner-fake
# and what vouches for a model a swap rebinds to
/lab/model-serving/model_store.json  @lab-owner-fake
/lab/model_roles.eval.json    @lab-owner-fake
/lab/model-evals/             @lab-owner-fake
# hooks and profiles that add tasks to a role's run
/lab/customizations/          @lab-owner-fake
# who may sign in over SSH: the certificate roles, their principals, TTLs and groups
/lab/ssh-ca.yml               @lab-owner-fake
# what must be sealed, and to whom
/.sops.yaml                   @lab-owner-fake
/.hnx-private-overlay.yml     @lab-owner-fake
